{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGaugeCovariance","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGaugeCovariance","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.TransverseSurfaceCurvature"],"declarations":51,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.trace_germ_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.trace_germ_conj","kind":"theorem","line":461,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GermConnectionGaugeCovariance.lean#L461-L474","doc":"**The trace of the germ IS gauge-invariant.** `τ(α(u))` survives the\nconnection law because the inhomogeneous term `(1 − Ad u) Θ` is\ntrace-annihilated.\n\nSubstrate reading: `τ(δq(w)) = q ∂_q log det ρ(w)`, which sees only\n`det ρ` — i.e. the abelianisation of the braid group, i.e. the writhe /\nframing. That is precisely the datum already walled by\n`no_writhe_only_framing`, so the surviving invariant linear functional of\nthe germ carries no new information. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.trace_adAct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.trace_adAct","kind":"theorem","line":454,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GermConnectionGaugeCovariance.lean#L454-L459","doc":"A cyclic trace is invariant under the adjoint action. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.cupSq_eq_neg_coboundary","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.cupSq_eq_neg_coboundary","kind":"theorem","line":434,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GermConnectionGaugeCovariance.lean#L434-L450","doc":"**THE COVARIANT SECOND-ORDER OBJECT IS A COBOUNDARY.**\n\n`α ∪ α = −∂β` with the **explicit** primitive `β = D ∘ α`. Hence the class\n`[α] ∪ [α] ∈ H²(G; R_{Ad})` — the canonical gauge-invariant second-order\nobject built from the germ — is **identically zero**, in every gauge and for\nevery representation.\n\n**Reading.** `D` differentiates in a *single* direction; a curvature needs\ntwo independent base directions, and the generator indices `i, j` of\n`⟦δq_i, δq_j⟧` are group elements, not directions. So the transverse\nNA-Stokes construction has no nonvanishing covariant order-2 content: the\nnaive `⟦δq_i, δq_j⟧` is not covariant (§4, §6), and the covariant\nreplacement vanishes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.secondGerm_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.secondGerm_mul","kind":"theorem","line":421,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GermConnectionGaugeCovariance.lean#L421-L432","doc":"The second germ fails the cocycle law by exactly the cup square. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.D_adAct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.D_adAct","kind":"theorem","line":405,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GermConnectionGaugeCovariance.lean#L405-L419","doc":"**A derivation fails to commute with the adjoint action by exactly one\nbracket against the germ**: `D(Ad_u x) = Ad_u(D x) + ⟦α(u), Ad_u x⟧`. This\nsingle identity is what makes the cup square a coboundary. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.secondGerm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.secondGerm","kind":"def","line":402,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GermConnectionGaugeCovariance.lean#L402-L403","doc":"The **second germ** `β = D ∘ α`. Substrate reading: `q ∂_q (q ∂_q ρ · ρ⁻¹)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.coboundary","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.coboundary","kind":"def","line":399,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GermConnectionGaugeCovariance.lean#L399-L400","doc":"The group coboundary of a 1-cochain `β`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.cupSq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.cupSq","kind":"def","line":393,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GermConnectionGaugeCovariance.lean#L393-L397","doc":"The bracket cup square of the germ 1-cocycle with itself:\n`(α ∪ α)(u,v) = ⟦α(u), Ad(u) α(v)⟧`. This — not `⟦α(u), α(v)⟧` — is the\ncanonical second-order object attached to a 1-cocycle, and it descends to\ncohomology classes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.germCurvature_not_covariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.germCurvature_not_covariant","kind":"theorem","line":384,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GermConnectionGaugeCovariance.lean#L384-L387","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.gaugeDefect_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.gaugeDefect_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":371,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GermConnectionGaugeCovariance.lean#L371-L382","doc":"**`germCurvature` IS NOT GAUGE-COVARIANT.** There is a ring, a derivation,\nand units for which the defect is nonzero — hence, by\n`germCurvature_covariant_iff`, the curvature is not a tensor.\n\nThis is the route-closing negative for the transverse NA-Stokes programme:\n`F_q = ⟦δq_i, δq_j⟧` has no basis-independent value, so neither does\n`Ω₂ = Σ J ⟦𝓕, 𝓕⟧` nor any norm of it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.gaugeDefect_witness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.gaugeDefect_witness","kind":"theorem","line":361,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GermConnectionGaugeCovariance.lean#L361-L369","doc":"**THE WITNESS.** With the gauge `b = u` (a genuinely `X`-dependent basis\nchange: `D b ≠ 0`), the covariance defect of the germ curvature is the\nexplicit nonzero matrix `!![X², −2X; 0, −X²]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.gaugeShift_uW_vW","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.gaugeShift_uW_vW","kind":"theorem","line":355,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GermConnectionGaugeCovariance.lean#L355-L359","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.gaugeShift_uW_uW","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.gaugeShift_uW_uW","kind":"theorem","line":349,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GermConnectionGaugeCovariance.lean#L349-L353","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.gaugePotential_uW","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.gaugePotential_uW","kind":"theorem","line":344,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GermConnectionGaugeCovariance.lean#L344-L347","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.germ_vW","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.germ_vW","kind":"theorem","line":339,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GermConnectionGaugeCovariance.lean#L339-L342","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.germ_uW","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.germ_uW","kind":"theorem","line":334,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GermConnectionGaugeCovariance.lean#L334-L337","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.vW","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.vW","kind":"def","line":326,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GermConnectionGaugeCovariance.lean#L326-L332","doc":"`v = !![1, 0; X, 1]`, the opposite unipotent unit; `α(v) = F`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.uW","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.uW","kind":"def","line":318,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GermConnectionGaugeCovariance.lean#L318-L324","doc":"`u = !![1, X; 0, 1]`, a unipotent unit; `α(u) = E`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.isDeriv_dW","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.isDeriv_dW","kind":"theorem","line":307,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GermConnectionGaugeCovariance.lean#L307-L316","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.dW","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.dW","kind":"def","line":304,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GermConnectionGaugeCovariance.lean#L304-L305","doc":"The witness derivation: entrywise `d/dX`. Substrate reading: `q ∂_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.W","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.W","kind":"def","line":300,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GermConnectionGaugeCovariance.lean#L300-L302","doc":"The witness ring: `2 × 2` matrices over `ℚ[X]`. Concrete counterexample\ncarrier only — no archimedean content (§7c). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.transversePairing_covariant_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.transversePairing_covariant_iff","kind":"theorem","line":285,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GermConnectionGaugeCovariance.lean#L285-L292","doc":"**The transverse pairing `Ω₂` is covariant iff the transported curvatures\nare unchanged.** Combined with §4 + §6: they are not, so `Ω₂` has no\nbasis-independent value, and neither does any norm of it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.listPairing_map_adAct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.listPairing_map_adAct","kind":"theorem","line":267,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GermConnectionGaugeCovariance.lean#L267-L283","doc":"Conjugation commutes with the ordered transverse pairing. So the pairing is\ncovariant **given** covariant inputs: every failure of covariance of `Ω₂`\ncomes from the curvature `F_q`, none of it from the transports (which are\nproducts of `ρ`'s, hence genuinely tensorial) or from the pairing itself. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.germCurvature_covariant_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.germCurvature_covariant_iff","kind":"theorem","line":254,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GermConnectionGaugeCovariance.lean#L254-L263","doc":"**COVARIANCE HOLDS IFF THE DEFECT VANISHES.** `germCurvature` is a tensor\nfor the gauge `b` exactly when `gaugeDefect D b u v = 0`. §6 exhibits a\nconcrete triple where it does not. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.germCurvature_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.germCurvature_conj","kind":"theorem","line":244,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GermConnectionGaugeCovariance.lean#L244-L252","doc":"**The transformation law of the germ curvature.** It picks up the defect\nadditively *inside* the conjugation: `F ↦ Ad(b)(F + Δ)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.gaugeDefect","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.gaugeDefect","kind":"def","line":238,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GermConnectionGaugeCovariance.lean#L238-L242","doc":"The obstruction to covariance of `germCurvature` under the gauge `b`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.germCurvature","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.germCurvature","kind":"def","line":235,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GermConnectionGaugeCovariance.lean#L235-L236","doc":"The germ `q`-curvature at two observers: `F_q = ⟦α(u), α(v)⟧`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.germ_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.germ_conj","kind":"theorem","line":216,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GermConnectionGaugeCovariance.lean#L216-L231","doc":"**THE CONNECTION LAW.**\n\nUnder the change of trivialisation `u ↦ b u b⁻¹` (a `q`-dependent change of\nrepresentation basis, `b = B(q)`), the germ transforms **inhomogeneously**:\n\n  `α(u) ↦ Ad(b) ( α(u) + (1 − Ad u) Θ )`,   `Θ = b⁻¹ (D b)`.\n\nThe extra term vanishes exactly when `D b = 0`, i.e. when the basis change\nis `q`-independent. The Hoefsmit seminormal basis and the reduced-Burau\nbasis are both `q`-dependent, and differ by such a `b`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.germ_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.germ_inv","kind":"theorem","line":210,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GermConnectionGaugeCovariance.lean#L210-L214","doc":"`α(b⁻¹) = −Θ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.germ_eq_adAct_gaugePotential","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.germ_eq_adAct_gaugePotential","kind":"theorem","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GermConnectionGaugeCovariance.lean#L203-L208","doc":"`α(b) = Ad(b) Θ` — the germ of the gauge element is its own potential,\nconjugated. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.gaugeShift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.gaugeShift","kind":"def","line":199,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GermConnectionGaugeCovariance.lean#L199-L201","doc":"The inhomogeneous shift `(1 − Ad u) Θ` picked up by the germ at `u`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.gaugePotential","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.gaugePotential","kind":"def","line":196,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GermConnectionGaugeCovariance.lean#L196-L197","doc":"The gauge potential of a `q`-dependent basis change `b`: `Θ = b⁻¹ (D b)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.germ_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.germ_mul","kind":"theorem","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GermConnectionGaugeCovariance.lean#L175-L192","doc":"**The germ is a 1-cocycle**: `α(uv) = α(u) + Ad(u) α(v)`. This is the\nstatement that `α` represents a class in `H¹(G; R_{Ad})` once one quotients\nby coboundaries — which §3 shows is exactly the gauge freedom. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.germ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.germ","kind":"def","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GermConnectionGaugeCovariance.lean#L171-L173","doc":"The **germ** (right logarithmic derivative) of a unit:\n`α(u) = (D u) u⁻¹`. Substrate reading: `δq_i = q (∂_q ρ(σ_i)) ρ(σ_i)⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.adAct_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.adAct_injective","kind":"theorem","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GermConnectionGaugeCovariance.lean#L166-L169","doc":"Conjugation is injective, so an identity of conjugates descends. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.adAct_inv_adAct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.adAct_inv_adAct","kind":"theorem","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GermConnectionGaugeCovariance.lean#L163-L164","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.adAct_comp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.adAct_comp","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GermConnectionGaugeCovariance.lean#L156-L161","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.adAct_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.adAct_one","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GermConnectionGaugeCovariance.lean#L153-L154","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.adAct_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.adAct_neg","kind":"theorem","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GermConnectionGaugeCovariance.lean#L150-L151","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.adAct_curvComm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.adAct_curvComm","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GermConnectionGaugeCovariance.lean#L146-L148","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.adAct_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.adAct_mul","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GermConnectionGaugeCovariance.lean#L137-L144","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.adAct_sub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.adAct_sub","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GermConnectionGaugeCovariance.lean#L134-L135","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.adAct_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.adAct_add","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GermConnectionGaugeCovariance.lean#L131-L132","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GermConnectionGauge.adAct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mas